[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-01-overview.png[/img]
[b]An HR manager for your colony.[/b] See how every colonist really spends their day, get work priorities suggested with the reasons, find the work that is falling behind, and run the whole colony from job titles you design yourself.

It adds one button to the bottom bar and one column to the Work tab. No new buildings, research or items.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/glance.png[/img]

[b]Required[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/workshop/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url]
[/list]

[b]Works with, when installed[/b]
[list]
[*][b][FSF] Complex Jobs[/b]: its split work types (smith, fabricate and so on) are tracked and advised separately.
[*][b]Vanilla Skills Expanded[/b]: expertise and its passions count toward how well a colonist fits a job.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-02-pages.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/pages.png[/img]

On the Time use page, click a category in the legend to hide it and recalculate from what is left. Whoever you have selected in the game is highlighted on every HR page.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-03-titles.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/titles.png[/img]

A title is a template, like "Doctor", "Crafter" or "Hauler". The advisor leaves title holders alone: it only tells you when someone is a poor fit for their title, or isn't doing its work, and why.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-04-advice.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/advice.png[/img]

[table]
[tr][th]Workload says[/th][th]It means[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]Keeping up[/td][td]Work arrives and gets done[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Slow / Falling behind[/td][td]Being worked, but the pile has lasted a day or is growing[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Needs more workers[/td][td]Steady work for two days and it still isn't shrinking[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Not being worked[/td][td]Nobody touched it in a day: fix the assignments[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]Open / Stuck bills[/td][td]Bills waiting at benches, or waiting with nobody working them[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-05-settings.png[/img]
Found in [b]Options > Mod Settings > SloppyMods - Human Resources[/b].
[list]
[*][b]Workbenches left out[/b]: untick a kind of workbench to leave all its bills out of the workload analysis.
[*][b]Bills left out[/b]: untick single bills. Use it for standing bills that only have work now and then, like recycling, so they aren't reported as stuck.
[/list]
On the HR tab itself, and saved with each game:
[list]
[*][b]Badges on portraits[/b] (on): a small coloured badge on each colonist portrait showing what they are doing.
[*][b]Daily review[/b] (off): re-check work assignments once a day and report what changed.
[*][b]Rest unused work[/b] (off): switch off work the colony has had none of for three days, and switch it back on when some appears.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-06-faq.png[/img]
[b]Which game versions does it support?[/b]
RimWorld 1.7 only.

[b]Can I add it to an existing save?[/b]
Yes. Time tracking starts from the moment you add it, so the Time use and Workload pages need a day or two before they say much.

[b]Can I remove it mid-save?[/b]
Yes. Your colonists keep whatever work priorities they have. The game will log a one-time error about the missing HR data, which is harmless.

[b]Will it change my work priorities on its own?[/b]
No. Nothing changes until you press Apply or assign a title. The daily review and resting unused work are both off until you turn them on.

[b]I changed a box on the Work tab and it has a * next to the title. Why?[/b]
That colonist holds a title and you set a box by hand. It is kept on top of their titles. Clear it on the HR tab under Job titles, Colonists.

[b]Two of my colonist's titles both use priority 1. Which goes first?[/b]
Both stay at 1, and the game picks between them left to right, the same as on the Work tab. Set one of them to 2 in its title if you want an order.

[b]A row says "Stuck bills" but nothing is wrong.[/b]
The bill has nothing to do right now. Press "Leave out..." on that row, or leave it out in the mod settings.

[b]Does it work with mods that change the Work tab?[/b]
It should. It adds an ordinary column and reads and writes ordinary work priorities. Tell me if the Title column is missing.

[b]Will it slow my game down?[/b]
It samples what each colonist is doing once a second and counts waiting work once an hour. The advisor only calculates while its page is open, or once a day if you turn the daily review on.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kanid99/SloppyMod-Rimworld-HumanResources/refs/heads/main/Workshop/banner-07-bugs.png[/img]
Every build shows its version number in the mod list. [b]Please include it[/b], plus your log, and I'll see what I can do.
Turn on Development mode, reproduce the problem and share your log. Lines from this mod start with [noparse][SloppyMods HR][/noparse].
